{"downsize method is defined twice; the second definition overwrites the first in Ruby, causing existing call sites that pass (max_width, max_height, opts) to raise ArgumentError due to wrong arity": 0.9028998017311096, "validateUploadedFile now hard-codes a 10MB limit for all uploads, ignoring max_image_size_kb/max_attachment_size_kb, breaking existing behavior and existing JS tests that expect the site setting to be enforced": 0.9906824827194214, "The downsizing loop ignores the return value from OptimizedImage.downsize. If the conversion fails, the loop will keep retrying and may leave an oversized (or partially written) file, then continue to Upload.create_for anyway": 0.9678561687469482, "The 413 handler reports a hard-coded 10MB limit, which can be incorrect if the instance allows larger uploads or if the failure relates to attachments, misleading users about the actual limit enforced by the server/proxy": 0.9580786228179932}